Yes! 🎯 Now I can see the exact bug. We do NOT need another screenshot.

In your server.js, the important line is:

const activePlan = user.plan || plan || "Free";
❌ This is the problem

Your database/user object has user.plan as Free.

Because JavaScript checks this first:

user.plan

it always chooses Free, even though the frontend sends:

Silver

That's why you get:

Free plan download limit reached.

✅ Exact fix

In server.js, find:

const activePlan = user.plan || plan || "Free";
Replace ONLY that line with:
const activePlan = plan || user.plan || "Free";

So it becomes:

// DETERMINE ACTIVE PLAN
const activePlan = plan || user.plan || "Free";


const planData = PLANS[activePlan];
