Yes. I found the actual problem now. You were not doing anything wrong.

Your uploaded App.jsx is corrupted in two places:

selectPlan() is opened and then another downloadVideo() function is inserted inside it.
Several JavaScript template strings are missing backticks, for example setMessage(Downloading ${video.title}...) and fetch(${API}/api/download...).
After the real export default App;, your file contains the old ChatGPT conversation text, so Vite tries to compile messages like "give correct code..." as JavaScript.
Your uploaded CSS has the same problem: it starts with conversation text instead of CSS.
✅ I fixed both files completely

Download the corrected App.jsx:

Download corrected App.jsx

Download the corrected App.css:

Download corrected App.css

I also removed the accidental duplicated functions and fixed the template strings, plan selection, download state, remaining quota, and button states.

